  "title": "Torsion-free integral homology for anchored configuration spaces of finite simple graphs",
  "batch_label": "70",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "disproved",
  "scope": "For every finite simple graph G, every subset K of its vertices, every integer n >= |K|, and every i >= 0, the integral homology group H_i(Sigma(G,K,n); Z) is free abelian, where Sigma is exactly the anchored configuration space of Definition 4.13 frozen in source.md. Consequently no cograph tuple (G,K,n,i) has nonzero integral homology torsion, so the frozen existential assertion is false.",
